# Part blocks: two answers from one parse.
#
# Every Advent of Code day asks two questions about the same input, and the
# parse above the Parts happens once. A Part branches from the current value
# like a Channel does, but labels what its body Reveals instead of storing it
# under a name — and it is a passthrough, so sibling Parts each see the same
# upstream list.
#
#   domain examples/17_two_parts.domain
#   Expected output:
#     Part 1: 24000
#     Part 2: 45000
Cursed Energy: 17_two_parts.input
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n\n"
Cursed Technique: Split Each by "\n"
Channeled Energy: Convert Each List to Integers
Maximum Technique: Sum Each Group

Part "1":
    Maximum Technique: Max
    Reveal: stdout

Part "2":
    Domain Expansion: Quicksort, Descending
    Maximum Technique: Select Top 3, Sum
    Reveal: stdout
